Review probes (PR #314, Review R): routes to Node's loader, to native
bindings or to evaluation that were reported verified. Every member route
to a require function, any module.<name> but exports, any eval, Function or
Reflect name or property, a computed property of the global object, the
Function constructor reached through constructor.constructor, the AsyncFunction
constructor, the CommonJS wrapper's arguments, the global
object passed as a value (Reflect.get(globalThis, …)), native
bindings, AMD define and the worker, child-process and cluster modules
are unverified. A static require.resolve of another node is a violation.
